WEBVTT

1
00:00:18.211 --> 00:00:19.912
your lemonade," Henry said.

2
00:00:20.893 --> 00:00:24.015
He handed a cup of ice-cold lemonade to a teenage girl.

3
00:00:24.035 --> 00:00:27.697
"Please come again," Henry's cousin Maggie added.

4
00:00:27.717 --> 00:00:31.720
"And let us know if you have any mysteries for us to solve."

5
00:00:32.828 --> 00:00:35.630
"Okay." The girl took a sip of her lemonade.

6
00:00:35.651 --> 00:00:39.173
"But nothing mysterious ever happens here in Belltown."

7
00:00:40.615 --> 00:00:41.335
Henry grinned.

8
00:00:41.355 --> 00:00:43.617
"That's what you think!"

9
00:00:44.057 --> 00:00:44.518
he said.

10
00:00:44.538 --> 00:00:49.402
"The Lemonade Detectives have solved five mysteries so far."

11
00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:53.405
He pointed to two signs on the lemonade stand.

12
00:00:54.866 --> 00:00:57.388
One of the signs was about the lemonade they were selling.

13
00:00:58.509 --> 00:01:01.612
The other sign was about The Lemonade Detective Agency.

14
00:01:02.792 --> 00:01:07.614
Henry, Maggie, and their friend Cole had started the agency a couple of weeks ago.

15
00:01:09.055 --> 00:01:11.436
At first it had been just a lemonade stand.

16
00:01:12.536 --> 00:01:16.978
Maggie had started selling lemonade to earn money for horseback-riding lessons.

17
00:01:18.178 --> 00:01:22.880
Her parents had promised to pay half of her lesson fees, but she had to pay the rest

18
00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:27.782
herself. Maggie's lemonade stand had been a big success from the start.

19
00:01:28.963 --> 00:01:31.884
On her very first day, she'd made a lot of money.

20
00:01:33.272 --> 00:01:36.053
But then the money had disappeared from her cashbox!

21
00:01:37.814 --> 00:01:41.155
Henry and Cole had helped her figure out who had taken it.

22
00:01:42.396 --> 00:01:46.197
After that the three of them had decided to open the detective agency.

23
00:01:47.378 --> 00:01:49.259
The teenage girl looked at the signs.

24
00:01:49.279 --> 00:01:51.119
"Oh right.

25
00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:56.482
I heard you helped my neighbor figure out how a groundhog was getting into his garden.

26
00:01:58.022 --> 00:02:01.784
That doesn't sound like a very exciting mystery to me," the girl went on.

27
00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:05.782
"But if anything mysterious happens, I'll let you know."

28
00:02:05.802 --> 00:02:08.303
"Okay," Henry said.

29
00:02:08.323 --> 00:02:10.364
"Enjoy your lemonade."

30
00:02:10.384 --> 00:02:15.567
"Thanks." The teenage girl took another sip, and then walked away.

31
00:02:15.587 --> 00:02:19.089
"She's right, you know," Maggie told Henry.

32
00:02:19.109 --> 00:02:22.671
"Our last few mysteries have been kind of boring."

33
00:02:22.691 --> 00:02:25.853
"I know," Henry said.

34
00:02:25.873 --> 00:02:27.794
"Finding Mr.

35
00:02:27.854 --> 00:02:30.516
Flinn's lost keys wasn't very interesting.

36
00:02:31.832 --> 00:02:35.853
Neither was the groundhog case, or the one about the missing library book.

37
00:02:36.973 --> 00:02:40.974
But we still got paid our detective fee each time, so we shouldn't complain."

38
00:02:42.055 --> 00:02:43.795
"That's true," Maggie agreed.

39
00:02:43.815 --> 00:02:50.997
"If we solve a few more cases, and keep selling lots of lemonade, I'll have enough money for

40
00:02:51.077 --> 00:02:52.097
lessons soon."

41
00:02:53.758 --> 00:02:56.919
She dropped the quarter from the teenage girl into the cashbox.

42
00:02:58.119 --> 00:03:01.400
"That's another 25 cents for my horseback-riding fund."

43
00:03:02.472 --> 00:03:06.275
"You mean one-third of 25 cents," Henry corrected her.

44
00:03:06.295 --> 00:03:09.338
"You have to split the money with Cole and me."

45
00:03:10.859 --> 00:03:11.900
Maggie shook her head.

46
00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:16.183
"Cole doesn't get to split the lemonade money when he's not here.

47
00:03:17.344 --> 00:03:20.067
So I get to keep one-half of 25 cents."

48
00:03:20.167 --> 00:03:24.070
"Oops, you're right," Henry said.

49
00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:28.153
"I forgot that Cole has swim-team tryouts again today."

50
00:03:28.173 --> 00:03:31.416
"Why does he want to be on the swim team?"

51
00:03:31.828 --> 00:03:32.608
Maggie wondered.

52
00:03:32.628 --> 00:03:38.991
"Hanging out at the lemonade stand seems a lot more fun than swimming laps all day long."

53
00:03:39.011 --> 00:03:42.853
"Cole loves sports," Henry reminded her.

54
00:03:42.873 --> 00:03:45.614
"And he's a really good swimmer."

55
00:03:45.634 --> 00:03:50.356
"He's lucky that someone on the team just moved away," Maggie said.

56
00:03:50.376 --> 00:03:54.637
"Otherwise he wouldn't have a chance to try out until next summer."

57
00:03:55.798 --> 00:03:56.538
Henry nodded.

58
00:03:56.558 --> 00:04:00.960
"Cole is the youngest kid trying to make the team," he said.

59
00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:05.161
"But it sounds like he did really well on the first day of tryouts.

60
00:04:06.401 --> 00:04:07.422
I bet he'll make the team."

61
00:04:08.722 --> 00:04:12.823
"I know why he's such a good swimmer," Maggie said with a laugh.

62
00:04:14.543 --> 00:04:16.224
"Why?" Henry asked her.

63
00:04:16.244 --> 00:04:21.565
"Because he spends so much time watching his pet frogs swim around their tank!"

64
00:04:22.666 --> 00:04:23.406
Henry grinned.

65
00:04:24.486 --> 00:04:27.367
Cole was crazy about reptiles and amphibians.

66
00:04:28.567 --> 00:04:30.828
He had several large tanks in his bedroom.

67
00:04:32.128 --> 00:04:33.989
One tank was full of frogs.

68
00:04:36.631 --> 00:04:40.193
Another tank was for his turtles, and a third one held a snake.

69
00:04:41.394 --> 00:04:44.136
Cole took very good care of all his pets.

70
00:04:44.156 --> 00:04:47.818
"Yeah," Henry said, still smiling.

71
00:04:47.838 --> 00:04:51.880
"Frogs are good swimmers, and so is Cole!"

72
00:04:52.981 --> 00:04:54.682
"Hey, here comes Cole now."

73
00:04:55.903 --> 00:04:57.264
Maggie pointed down the street.

74
00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:03.223
Henry was surprised to see Cole running toward them from the direction of the town pool.

75
00:05:03.243 --> 00:05:07.026
"I wonder why he's back so soon," Henry said.

76
00:05:07.046 --> 00:05:10.228
"Tryouts just started a few minutes ago.

77
00:05:11.249 --> 00:05:12.750
They shouldn't be over for hours."

78
00:05:13.990 --> 00:05:14.731
Maggie shrugged.

79
00:05:14.751 --> 00:05:18.534
"Maybe the coach already told him that he didn't make the team."

80
00:05:18.554 --> 00:05:22.877
"I doubt it," Henry said, still watching Cole.

81
00:05:22.897 --> 00:05:26.319
"I don't think they even started swimming yet today.

82
00:05:27.540 --> 00:05:29.085
Look! Cole's hair isn't wet."

83
00:05:29.105 --> 00:05:34.789
"That's a smart observation, Detective Henry," Maggie said with a laugh.

84
00:05:36.090 --> 00:05:37.411
Cole was closer by now.

85
00:05:38.532 --> 00:05:40.513
Henry could see that he was very upset.

86
00:05:42.174 --> 00:05:42.895
"What's wrong?"

87
00:05:43.315 --> 00:05:44.016
Henry asked.

88
00:05:45.237 --> 00:05:46.377
"Why aren't you at the pool?"

89
00:05:47.518 --> 00:05:50.300
Cole skidded to a stop in front of the lemonade stand.

90
00:05:50.320 --> 00:05:54.063
"I need your help!"

91
00:05:54.483 --> 00:05:54.964
he cried.

92
00:05:56.253 --> 00:06:00.657
"Someone dumped a bunch of frogs into the pool right before tryouts started.

93
00:06:08.665 --> 00:06:10.768
And everyone thinks I'm the one who did it!"
